            "original": "'horizontal' | 'vertical'",
            "resolved": "\"horizontal\" | \"vertical\"",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Layout orientation:\n - 'horizontal' (default): index axis runs left→right, value axis bottom→top.\n - 'vertical': index axis runs top→bottom (one cell per data point, fixed\n   `rowHeight`), value axis left→right. Built to sit beside an external list\n   of the SAME row height so row i lines up with point i. The SVG's height is\n   count*rowHeight; place it in a non-scaling, slim column and let the parent\n   scroll it in lockstep with the list."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        },
        {
          "name": "rowHeight",
          "type": "number",
          "attribute": "row-height",
          "reflect": false,
          "mutable": false,
          "required": false,
          "optional": false,
          "defaultValue": "44",
          "complexType": {
            "original": "number",
            "resolved": "number",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Vertical mode: per-row height in px (match the list's row pitch)."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        },
        {
          "name": "vbWidth",
          "type": "number",
          "attribute": "vb-width",
          "reflect": false,
          "mutable": false,
          "required": false,
          "optional": false,
          "defaultValue": "80",
          "complexType": {
            "original": "number",
            "resolved": "number",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Vertical mode: the viewBox WIDTH in px. Because the vertical chart uses\n`preserveAspectRatio=\"none\"`, the host should render the SVG at THIS same CSS\nwidth (e.g. `flex: 0 0 150px`) so the x-axis is 1:1 and value-label text is\ncrisp (not horizontally stretched). Default 80 keeps the pre-existing slim\nstrip behaviour for callers that don't opt into labels."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        },
        {
          "name": "showValueLabels",
          "type": "boolean",
          "attribute": "show-value-labels",
          "reflect": false,
          "mutable": false,
          "required": false,
          "optional": false,
          "defaultValue": "false",
          "complexType": {
            "original": "boolean",
            "resolved": "boolean",
            "references": {}
          },
          "docs": {
            "tags": [],
            "text": "Vertical mode: render per-point VALUE LABELS + point dots so the temp /\nhumidity readings are legible on their own (not just a line smear). The first\nLINE series on the LEFT axis is labelled in the left gutter (°), the first on\nthe RIGHT axis in the right gutter (%). Additive — off by default."
          },
          "internal": false,
          "getter": false,
          "setter": false
        }
